## Objection cards: business persona
| They say | You say (≤ 20 seconds) | Proof to point at |
|---|---|---|
| "It's synthetic. Why believe the uplift?" | "You shouldn't, yet. The business case applies *rates* measured on a hold-out to UK Finance and PSR baselines, never synthetic totals, and the pilot re-measures on your data before anything touches a customer." | Deck slide 5; `business_case` basis column |
| "My team can't take more alerts." | "Same number of holds. If you'd rather, the model matches today's catch with {{K_MATCH}} holds instead of {{RULES_ALERTS}}: {{ALERT_REDUCTION}}% fewer." | Results table |
| "What if we block genuine customers?" | "Genuine holds per scam fall from {{FP_RULES}} to {{FP_MODEL}}. Every hold has plain-English reasons; the GenAI message is drafted for an analyst to approve." | Live check: genuine invoice released |
| "How confident are you in {{NET_VALUE}}?" | "The range is {{SENS_LOW}} to {{SENS_HIGH}}. Even the conservative case (lower market share, 40% intervention success, higher run cost) pays back many times over." | `business_case_sensitivity` |
| "Vulnerable customers?" | "Vulnerability is a model feature *and* a queue attribute. Impersonation scripts are written for older and vulnerable customers." | Case note in the queue |
| "Why not buy a vendor scam score?" | "A vendor score is a good *feature*; we'd ingest it. It won't give you your own claims labels, your own analyst feedback loop, or one governed view across fraud, finance and conduct." | Lakehouse Sync loop |
| "How fast?" | "Six weeks to a signed-off business case on your data." | Deck slide 10 |
| "What's the catch?" | "Two honest ones: absolute rates will differ on real data, and very small, perfectly coached purchase scams can still pass. That's why claims feed back into retraining." | `evidence/app_session.md` residual-risk case |

## Objection cards: technical persona
| They say | You say | Proof |
|---|---|---|
| "Training/serving skew: the app rebuilds features." | "Known prototype trade-off. `build_features` mirrors the gold SQL one-to-one. Production moves to UC Feature Engineering with online feature serving so batch and online share one definition." | Decision #14 |
| "Latency for Faster Payments?" | "Measured: three Lakebase point lookups p50 {{PG_P50}} ms; Model Serving ~100 ms round-trip. GenAI only runs when we're already holding the payment." | `evidence/job_run/publish_to_lakebase.md`, `deploy_model_serving.md` |
| "Why Lakebase, not the warehouse?" | "Single-row reads and *transactional* writes (decision + status in one commit). A warehouse is built for scans. Synced tables and Lakehouse Sync remove ETL both ways." | Trace step 7–8 |
| "Leakage?" | "Windows look strictly backwards, the split is by time, labels only come from claims (which arrive late), and immature days are excluded." | `03_gold.sql`, training notebook |
| "Isn't 0.99 ROC-AUC suspicious?" | "ROC-AUC is inflated by millions of easy negatives; the honest metric is PR-AUC {{PR_AUC}} and value recall at a fixed budget. Our first version hit 0.9995 and we threw it out as unrealistic." | `docs/ai-assisted-build.md` #5 |
| "Model risk / SS1/23?" | "UC registry with aliases, evaluation tables, lineage from raw file to score, inference tables logging every live call. Champion/challenger is an alias switch." | `platform_queries.md` §9, §11, §21 |
| "PII and the LLM?" | "Masked in Unity Catalog *before* data reaches the LLM, Genie or Lakebase. The LLM sees masked names and behavioural features only, inside the Databricks boundary." | Trace step 3 + 7 |
| "How do the reason codes stay honest?" | "They're value-aware ('payee added 24 days ago', not a generic label). We found a mismatch by tracing one payment end to end and fixed it in the model." | `evidence/trace_one_payment.md` |
| "Scale to 190M payments/yr?" | "Serverless pipeline with Photon; real-time scoring is stateless behind an autoscaling endpoint; Lakebase autoscales." | Architecture doc |
| "Hallucination in case notes?" | "Prompt contains only structured facts; output is schema-constrained JSON; the action is advisory; parse failures are logged, never fatal. The next step is MLflow evaluation with Guidelines judges." | Decision #9, #20 |

## If something breaks live
* Model endpoint cold → "it scales to zero overnight; in production we pin a replica during banking hours". Then show `evidence/app_session.md` §12.
* App or SSO issue → walk the trace: `evidence/trace_one_payment.md` tells the whole story with real data, hop by hop.
* Genie slow → read Q1/Q2 from `evidence/genie_transcripts.md`.

## Rehearsal drill (do it, don't read it)
1. **Pass 1, timing:** run the 12-minute version out loud with a timer. Cut words until it fits in 11.
2. **Pass 2, the 60-second version** three times, with no notes.
3. **Pass 3, objections:** have someone (or an AI roleplay) fire 5 random cards from each table; answer in ≤ 20 seconds, then point at the proof.
4. **Tech check 10 minutes before:** open the app, run one live check (warms Model Serving), leave one CRITICAL alert OPEN, have `evidence/trace_one_payment.md` open in a tab.
